## File naming conventions

| Layer | Pattern | Example |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Complete notes | `Module_NN_{Title}.md` | `Module_01_Contracts_of_Indemnity.md` |
| Condensed notes | `Module_NN_to_MM_Condensed.md` | `Module_01_to_04_Condensed.md` |
| Comparison tables | `{A}_vs_{B}.md` | `Indemnity_vs_Guarantee.md` |
| Question bank | `Q{NN}_{Topic}.md` | `Q01_Unpaid_Seller.md` |
| Distinguish | `Q{NN}_{A}_Vs_{B}.md` | `Q01_Indemnity_Vs_Guarantee.md` |

---

## Output location rule

All generated content MUST stay under **`.temp/{subject-slug}/`**. Do NOT write to `Academics/` or other repo paths unless the user explicitly overrides.

---

## Strict prohibitions

Never:
- Create debug files, raw metadata dumps, or temporary logs as deliverables.
- Generate off-syllabus topic trees without flagging inference.
- Hallucinate legal material.
- Ignore syllabus hierarchy when a syllabus exists.
- Generate question banks with questions only (no model answers).
- Generate fewer than 5 Q&A files per mark folder.

